---
name: sonner
type: registry:ui
title: Sonner
description: An opinionated toast component for Svelte, themed to match the design system.
dependencies:
  - svelte-sonner
  - mode-watcher
  - "@lucide/svelte"
files:
  - path: registry/items/components/sonner/index.ts
    type: registry:ui
    target: "~/components/sonner/index.ts"
  - path: registry/items/components/sonner/sonner.svelte
    type: registry:ui
    target: "~/components/sonner/sonner.svelte"
---

Use sonner for toast notifications. Mount `Toaster` once near the root of your app, then call `toast`
from `svelte-sonner` anywhere. Theme follows [mode-watcher](https://github.com/svecosystem/mode-watcher);
status icons come from lucide.

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import { toast } from 'svelte-sonner';
	import { Toaster } from '~/components/sonner';
	import { Button } from '~/components/button';
</script>

<Toaster />
<Button
	variant="outline"
	onclick={() =>
		toast('Event has been created', {
			description: 'Sunday, December 03, 2023 at 9:00 AM',
			action: {
				label: 'Undo',
				onClick: () => console.info('Undo')
			}
		})}
>
	Show Toast
</Button>
```
